IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Exemption from sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35) Notification (Cap. 323, N 1), made under section 73 of the
-- Act (section 96 in the 2020 Revised Edition): the Schedule's columns of authorised radio frequency bands and maximum approved field
-- strength or power, in every vintage deposited.  Texts: TA1999-N1 (2002 Revised Edition), its eight amending notifications on IMDA's list, and three the e-Gazette
-- supplied that IMDA's list does not include (S 115/2001, the Notification as made; S 525/2001, which is the Schedule the Revised Edition prints; and S 78/2017), under
-- subjects/sg/telecommunications-exemption-notification-2001/registers/source-bundle/.
-- sgta-i-n1-exemption.l4 models which EQUIPMENT each vintage names; this file models the bands and limits against the item numbers.
-- A band is written as the Schedule prints it, with each dash written as a hyphen and no spaces around it.  An entry is "band: limit",
-- or just "band" where the Schedule prints no limit (items 14 and 15 of the Revised Edition list receive-only frequencies).
-- Each amending notification replaces whole items, so each vintage's function answers for the items it replaces and defers to the earlier
-- vintage for the rest.  The IMDA copies of S 1/2008, S 265/2006 and S 179/2011 have four extraction defects, and the e-Gazette copies of the same
-- notifications (deposited 2026-11-04 beside them as TA1999-N1-S1-2008-GAZ.txt and so on) print the values this module uses: S 1/2008 item 3 reads
-- "57 dBµV/m @ 3m" (the IMDA copy reads "57 dBµ/Vm @ 3m"); S 179/2011 item 8 reads "25 µW" (the IMDA copy reads "25 W", S 1/2008 and S 252/2013 "25 µW");
-- the IMDA copies of S 265/2006 and S 1/2008 lose the decimal point in "240.15" and "10.50", which the Gazette copies print.  The `-- src:` quote lines
-- below are the IMDA lines, defects included, because the coverage rows and locators are those lines'; the values in the functions follow the Gazette.
-- A date before 2 March 2001 answers NOTHING, as in sgta-i-n1-exemption.l4: the Notification as made, S 115/2001, came into operation on 2 March 2001.  (NOTES.md finding 23 records the correction of the two values.)

§ `N 1 Schedule (2002 Revised Edition)`

