@ref N 1 Schedule (2002 Revised Edition) (src:TA1999-N1:36-158)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`N 1 Schedule (2002 Revised Edition): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING
           IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (LIST "477.000-477.250 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (LIST "0.51-1.60 MHz: 57 dBµV/m @ 3m", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 65 dBµV/m @ 10m", "88.00-108.00 MHz: 60 dBµV/m @ 10m", "180.000-200.000 MHz: 112 dBµV/m @ 10m", "487.000-507.000 MHz: 112 dBµV/m @ 10m")
           IF item EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 5 THEN JUST (LIST "0.016-0.150 MHz: 100 dBµV/m @ 3m")
           IF item EQUALS 6 THEN JUST (LIST "151.125 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "151.150 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 7 THEN JUST (LIST "0.016-0.150 MHz: 100 dBµV/m @ 3m", "13.553-13.567 MHz: 94 dBµV/m @ 10m", "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "146.350-146.500 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "240.150-240.300 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "300.000-300.300 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "314.700-315.000 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "444.400-444.800 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "868.10-869.00 MHz: 65 dBµV/m @ 10m", "10.50-10.55 GHz: 117dBµV/m @ 10m")
           IF item EQUALS 8 THEN JUST (LIST "40.500-41.000 MHz: 0.01 mW ERP", "454.000-454.500 MHz: 2 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 9 THEN JUST (LIST "72.080 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.200 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.400 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.600 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "158.275/162.875 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "158.325/162.925 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "453.7250/458.7250 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "453.7375/458.7375 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "453.7500/458.7500 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "453.7625/458.7625 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 10 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "29.700-30.000 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 11 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (LIST "1.605-1.800 MHz: 94 dBµV/m@ 3m", "40.00-40.50 MHz: 57 dBµV/m@ 3m", "46.50-47.00 MHz: 90 dBµV/m @ 3m", "49.50-50.00 MHz: 90 dBµV/m @ 3m", "1,880.00-1,900 MHz: 250 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 13 THEN JUST (LIST "433.79-434.79 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "866.10-869.00 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "819.00-823.00 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "924.00-925.00 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "1,880.00-1,900.00 MHz: 250 mW EIRP", "2,400.00-2,483.50 MHz: 100 mW EIRP", "5,150.00-5,250.00 MHz: 100 mW EIRP", "5,725.00-5,875.00 MHz: 100 mW EIRP", "18,820-18,870 MHz: 500 mW EIRP", "19,160-19,210 MHz: 500 mW EIRP", "24,000-24,250 MHz: 100 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 14 THEN JUST (LIST "1,575.420 MHz")
           IF item EQUALS 15 THEN JUST (LIST "2,505.250 MHz", "2,521.250 MHz", "2,537.250 MHz", "2,553.250 MHz", "2,569.250 MHz", "2,601.250 MHz", "2,617.250 MHz", "2,633.250 MHz", "2,649.250 MHz", "2,665.250 MHz")
           IF item EQUALS 16 THEN JUST (LIST "76.00-77.00 GHz: 5W EIRP for vehicle in motion 250 mW EIRP for stationary vehicle")
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `N 1 Schedule as made by S 115/2001 (2 March 2001)`

-- The Notification as made: a 15-item Schedule headed "EXEMPTION IN RESPECT OF IN-BUILDING OR LOCALISED ON-SITE OPERATION OF EQUIPMENT", with the limit column printed
-- "Strength (dB) (µV/m) or power (mW)" and the entries "dB @ 3m" and "dB @ 10m" (S 525/2001 prints "dBµV/m @ 3m" and "dBµV/m @ 10m"); each value is keyed as printed here.
-- The two bands marked "**" in item 13 are "For in-building operations only" (TA1999-N1-S115-2001.txt:174).  The band and limit lines below are every Schedule line
-- (page furniture left out); the numbers carry no thousands comma in item 6, item 9 and item 15 ("1000 mW ERP", "2505.250 MHz"), as printed.  Item 16 does not exist yet.
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:30 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:31 | (Exemption from sections 33, 34 (1) (b) and 35) Notification 2001 and
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:32 | shall come into operation on 2nd March 2001.
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:34 | Exemption
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:35 | 2. Sections 33, 34 (1) (b) and 35 of the Act shall not apply to any
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:36 | person in respect of —
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:37 | (a) the possession, establishment, installation, maintenance,
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:38 | provision or operation of any network or station as defined
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:39 | in the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:40 | Regulations 2001 (G.N. No. S 114/2001) where the person
-- src:TA1999-N1-S115-2001:41 | has been permitted by the Authority to use any radio
