-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:134 | 13. Wireless LAN, RFID 13.553 – 13.567 MHz 10 mW ERP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:135 | or Low Power Devices
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:136 | 433.05 – 434.79 MHz 10 mW ERP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:138 | 866.00 – 869.00 MHz 500 mW ERP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:140 | 917.00 – 925.00 MHz 500 mW ERP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:142 | 1,880.00 – 1,900.00 MHz 250 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:144 | 2,400.00 – 2,483.50 MHz 200 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:146 | 5,150.00 – 5,350.00 MHz 200 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:148 | 5,470.00 – 5,725.00 MHz 1 W EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:150 | 5,725.00 – 5,875.00 MHz 1 W EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:152 | 5,945.00 – 6,425.00 MHz 250 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:154 | 24,000 – 24,250 MHz 100 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:156 | 57,000 – 66,000 MHz 10 W EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:158 | 122.00 – 123.00 GHz 100 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:160 | 244.00 – 246.00 GHz 100 mW EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:162 | 14. Global Navigation 1,164 – 1,300 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:163 | Satellite Systems
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:164 | Receivers 1,559 – 1,610 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:166 | 15. Short Range Radar 76.00 – 77.00 GHz 55 dBm peak
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:167 | System EIRP
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:169 | 23.5 dBm average
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:170 | EIRP for pulse
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:171 | radar
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:173 | 50 dBm average
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:174 | EIRP for other
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:175 | radar types
@ref N 1 First Schedule as amended by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023) (src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:41-175)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`N 1 First Schedule as amended by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (LIST "446.00-446.10 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "446.3250-446.4750 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (LIST "0.51-1.60 MHz: 57 dBμV/m @ 3m", "29.70-30.00 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 65 dBμV/m @ 10m", "88.00-108.00 MHz: 60 dBμV/m @ 10m", "180.00-200.00 MHz: 50 mW ERP", "470.00-534.00 MHz: 50 mW ERP", "487.00-507.00 MHz: 112 dBμV/m @ 10m", "534.00-614.00 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "614.00-698.00 MHz: 50 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 5 THEN JUST (LIST "0.016-0.150 MHz: 66 dBµA/m @ 10m", "0.150-5.000 MHz: 13.5 dBµA/m @ 10m", "6.765-6.795 MHz: 42 dBµA/m @ 10m", "7.400-8.800 MHz: 9 dBµA/m @ 10m", "10.200-11.000 MHz: 9 dBuA/m @ 10m")
           IF item EQUALS 8 THEN JUST (LIST "9.000-315.000 kHz: 30 dBµA/m @ 10m", "40.500-41.000 MHz: 0.01 mW ERP", "216.00-217.00 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "All other frequencies: 25 µW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 9 THEN JUST (LIST "72.080 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.200 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.400 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "72.600 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "158.275/162.875 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP", "158.325/162.925 MHz: 1,000 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 10 THEN JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 11 THEN JUST (LIST "26.960-27.280 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "34.995-35.225 MHz: 100 mW ERP", "40.660-40.700 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "72.130-72.210 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
           IF item EQUALS 12 THEN JUST (LIST "1,880.00-1,900.00 MHz: 250 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 13 THEN JUST (LIST "13.553-13.567 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "433.05-434.79 MHz: 10 mW ERP", "866.00-869.00 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "917.00-925.00 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "1,880.00-1,900.00 MHz: 250 mW EIRP", "2,400.00-2,483.50 MHz: 200 mW EIRP", "5,150.00-5,350.00 MHz: 200 mW EIRP", "5,470.00-5,725.00 MHz: 1 W EIRP", "5,725.00-5,875.00 MHz: 1 W EIRP", "5,945.00-6,425.00 MHz: 250 mW EIRP", "24,000-24,250 MHz: 100 mW EIRP", "57,000-66,000 MHz: 10 W EIRP", "122.00-123.00 GHz: 100 mW EIRP", "244.00-246.00 GHz: 100 mW EIRP")
           IF item EQUALS 14 THEN JUST (LIST "1,164-1,300 MHz", "1,559-1,610 MHz")
           IF item EQUALS 15 THEN JUST (LIST "76.00-77.00 GHz: 55 dBm peak EIRP; 23.5 dBm average EIRP for pulse radar; 50 dBm average EIRP for other radar types")
           OTHERWISE `N 1 First Schedule as amended by S 78/2017 (1 April 2017): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item

§ `N 1 Second Schedule as substituted by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023)`

-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:178 | Amendment of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:179 | 5. In the principal Notification, in the Second Schedule, replace
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:180 | items 1 to 3 with —
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:181 | “ 1. Fixed White Space Devices 174 – 188 MHz 4,000 mW EIRP for
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:182 | all authorised
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:183 | 195 – 202 MHz frequency bands
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:184 | 209 – 230 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:186 | 470 – 534 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:188 | 614 – 694 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:192 | 2. Portable Mode I White Space Devices 174 – 188 MHz 100 mW EIRP for all
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:193 | authorised frequency
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:194 | 195 – 202 MHz bands
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:195 | 209 – 230 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:197 | 470 – 534 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:199 | 614 – 694 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:201 | 3. Portable Mode II White Space Devices 174 – 188 MHz 100 mW EIRP for all
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:202 | authorised frequency
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:203 | 195 – 202 MHz bands
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:204 | 209 – 230 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:206 | 470 – 534 MHz
-- src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:208 | 614 – 694 MHz
@ref N 1 Second Schedule as substituted by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023) (src:TA1999-N1-S588-2023:178-208)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`N 1 Second Schedule as substituted by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (LIST "174-188 MHz: 4,000 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "195-202 MHz: 4,000 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "209-230 MHz: 4,000 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "470-534 MHz: 4,000 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "614-694 MHz: 4,000 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands")
           IF item EQUALS 2 OR item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (LIST "174-188 MHz: 100 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "195-202 MHz: 100 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "209-230 MHz: 100 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "470-534 MHz: 100 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands", "614-694 MHz: 100 mW EIRP for all authorised frequency bands")
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `N 1 Schedule on a date, and the Schedule's footnote`

-- src:TA1999-N1:161 | * Other low power equipment that operate in radio frequency bands other than those
-- src:TA1999-N1:162 | listed, but which meet the output power limits specified for the same type of equipment
-- src:TA1999-N1:163 | are exempted from licensing as long as both the output power limits and the radio
-- src:TA1999-N1:164 | frequency bands are approved by the Authority.
@ref N 1 Schedule footnote, 2002 Revised Edition (src:TA1999-N1:161-164)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`N 1 Schedule: the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n, on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 17 10 2001) THEN `N 1 Schedule as made by S 115/2001 (2 March 2001): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 1 2003) THEN `N 1 Schedule as substituted by S 525/2001 (17 October 2001): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 12 2003) THEN `N 1 Schedule (2002 Revised Edition): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 10 2004) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 591/2003 (15 December 2003): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 18 5 2006) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 651/2004 (28 October 2004): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 1 2008) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 265/2006 (18 May 2006): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2011) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 1/2008 (2 January 2008): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 25 4 2013) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 179/2011 (1 April 2011): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 23 6 2014) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 252/2013 (25 April 2013): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 11 2014) THEN `N 1 Schedule as amended by S 415/2014 (23 June 2014): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2017) THEN `N 1 First Schedule as substituted by S 726/2014 (1 November 2014): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 9 2023) THEN `N 1 First Schedule as amended by S 78/2017 (1 April 2017): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item
           OTHERWISE `N 1 First Schedule as amended by S 588/2023 (1 September 2023): the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n` item

GIVEN `the equipment is other low power equipment operating in a radio frequency band other than those listed for the same type of equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it meets the output power limit specified for the same type of equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved both the output power limit and the radio frequency band` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 Schedule footnote: the other low power equipment is exempted from licensing` MEANS
    `the equipment is other low power equipment operating in a radio frequency band other than those listed for the same type of equipment`
    AND `it meets the output power limit specified for the same type of equipment`
    AND `the Authority approved both the output power limit and the radio frequency band`
